    "/v1/recipient/consents/start": {
      "post": {
        "tags": [
          "fdx"
        ],
        "summary": "`POST /v1/recipient/consents/start` — start consent authorization.\nThe two-ledger recipient flow (fdx DESIGN.md §1 + §4 consent-flow\nsequence): the recipient-side fdx instance writes its OWN registry\n(a `pending` row in `recipient_consents`, in the recipient tenant),\nensures its per-provider OAuth client exists at the provider's\nauthorization server (DCR, cached in `fdx.recipients`), and pushes a\nPAR request whose `state` carries `\"<consent handle>|<app origin>\"`.\nThe AS's authorize screen runs the ceremony; the browser redirect\ncomes back to THIS instance's `/fdx/consents/callback` (the\nregistered redirect_uri), which activates the row and exchanges the\ncode. The provider's grant row is seeded by the provider's OWN\nauth-family consumer from `sentin8:auth:grant:created` — never by\nthis side.",
        "operationId": "start_consent",
        "requestBody": {
          "content": {
            "application/json": {
              "schema": {
                "$ref": "#/components/schemas/StartConsentRequest"
              }
            }
          },
          "required": true
        },
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Consent started with authorization URL",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {}
              }
            }
          },
          "403": {
            "description": "Missing fdx:read scope"
          }
        },
        "security": [
          {
            "fdx:read": []
          }
        ]
      }
    },
